# THE PLOUGH (src/core/sentinel/designs/plough.gd): the Snowfield's keeper at eye
# level, on its own ground. It ploughs its way through the drifts at the player,
# leaving pale furrows of packed ice behind it; on its lanes it runs, and a run
# carried off one into the snow bogs and stalls it (tests/sentinel/test_plough.gd).
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/plough.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 --held=axe_felling --config=unharmed
coast calm
place snowfield
near keeper
wait 0.6
await sentinel 12
# Woken, then stood off in the drift: it ploughs its way through at the player,
# slow. (A frame by its side is taken from inside the share: a wide body wants
# the stand-off.)
walkto mob 8
walk 0,1 2.5
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
try 4
  await tell 14
end
wait 0.2
shot 01-it-ploughs-through-the-drift-at-you with shoulder,mob:sentinel.snowfield
